    {
      "post_id": "91253",
      "author_handle": "Nic21k",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 7 years 11 months ago",
      "body": "Hi. I’ve never been on here before but looking for a bit of help. My little girl is nearly 11 months old and has always been breastfed. As I’m returning to work in January I want to start getting her used to a bottle now so I know she will be ok when I am not home. I will be working 12 hour shifts, day and night. However I find expressing so difficult!! No matter how long I express for, I get very little milk. I’ve tried different pumps but still have the same issue. I can get about 2oz in 30 minutes and then it just stops. Is this normal? Is there anything I can do to get more milk or to speed it up? I don’t know how I’m ever going to get enough to leave for while I’m not here",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10762/#91253",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/a7655c1a99e7b2fc1abd.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10762/",
      "role": "original_post",
      "original_post_id": "91253"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "91254",
      "author_handle": "qiaraau",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 7 years 11 months ago",
      "body": "Hi 🙂 I think you should rest more. Also you should improve your diet. Eat more veggies and and fruits. Stay health and your body will follow. 🙂",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10762/#91254",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/a7655c1a99e7b2fc1abd.html",
