    },
    {
      "post_id": "91843",
      "author_handle": "Nancyval",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 6 years 7 months ago",
      "body": "Well this might be useless to the original question, but might be useful for other.\nIn a situation like this i will suggest you take more water and pump after breastfeeding. When you're sure your baby is well fed and you still have some milk left in your breast, pump it all until it is emptied... Try pumping in the morning and also at night before going to bed\nAll this will get your body used to pump ..",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10762/#91843",
